# .trivyignore -- D-07 (plan 11-02, Task 3 live verification, 2026-08-23).
#
# publish.yml's trivy-action step (severity: HIGH,CRITICAL, exit-code: 1,
# ignore-unfixed: true) scans all three published images identically
# (csv-processor, dbt, airflow). Investigating a first real CI-shaped run
# (`docker build` + `aquasec/trivy:0.73.0 image` locally against the exact
# images `make image-csv-processor`/`image-dbt`/`image-airflow` produce, git
# SHA a30740e) found:
#
#   - csv-processor: 0 HIGH/CRITICAL findings. Clean, no entry needed.
#   - dbt: 3 HIGH findings, all in `sqlparse 0.5.5` (CVE-2026-54284,
#     CVE-2026-59893, CVE-2026-71491), FIXED in sqlparse 0.6.0. Cause:
#     dbt-core==1.12.2 pins `sqlparse<0.6.0,>=0.5.5`, making 0.6.0
#     uninstallable at that pin. A same-day dbt-core patch release, 1.12.3
#     (verified live via `pip index versions dbt-core` inside the built
#     image), relaxes the pin to `sqlparse<0.7.0,>=0.5.5`. Fixed by bumping
#     `docker/dbt/Dockerfile`'s pin to dbt-core==1.12.3 (a real upstream fix
#     existed, so this is a version bump, not a suppression) -- re-scanned
#     clean (0 findings) after the bump. No .trivyignore entry needed for
#     dbt either.
#   - airflow: every one of the findings below. Confirmed via a direct
#     `trivy image ... apache/airflow:3.3.0-python3.12` scan of the
#     untouched upstream base image (no local modifications) that the
#     finding COUNT is byte-identical (4 Java / 36 Python / 1+1 rustbinary /
#     8 gobinary = same totals, same CVE IDs) to `airflow:a30740e`, this
#     project's own built image. `docker/airflow/Dockerfile` adds exactly
#     two things on top of that base: `apache-airflow[otel]==3.3.0`
#     (installed under Airflow's own official, pinned
#     constraints-3.3.0/constraints-3.12.txt -- overriding any single
#     package version here would mean deviating from Airflow's own
#     tested/supported dependency set, the same determinism rationale the
#     Dockerfile's own header comment already establishes) and
#     `psycopg[binary]==3.3.4` (already the newest pinned release used
#     project-wide). Neither addition is implicated in any finding below --
#     every affected package (GitPython, aiohttp, cryptography, litellm,
#     pyasn1, sqlparse, the Java jars bundled inside the `ray` package,
#     quinn-proto inside `uv`/`uvx`, and Go stdlib inside the bundled
#     `/usr/bin/docker` CLI) is already present, at the same version, in the
#     stock `apache/airflow:3.3.0-python3.12` image as published by the
#     Apache Airflow project. None are reachable/fixable from this
#     repository's own Dockerfile without forking Airflow's own official
#     image or its constraints file -- out of scope for this CI/CD
#     publish-pipeline plan. Recorded here, dated, so the gate this plan
#     built (D-10: PR and merge images scanned identically) can still pass
#     on real content this repo does not control, rather than either
#     silently disabling the gate or blocking every future publish run on
#     upstream's own unfixed base image.

# --- Java (ray_dist.jar, bundled inside the `ray` package in the upstream
#     apache/airflow:3.3.0-python3.12 base image) ---
